<title>USA: Mich. Senate advances gas tax hike for roads.</title>
<headline>Mich. Senate advances gas tax hike for roads.</headline>
<dateline>LANSING, Mich. 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Michigan Senate has approved a gasoline tax increase to fund road repairs, but did not include a state takeover of local roads sought by Gov. John Engler, a budget spokeswoman said Thursday.</p>
<p>Senators approved the 4 cent-per-gallon increase Wednesday and moved it to the House for consideration, said Maureen McNulty, spokeswoman for the Michigan Department of Management and Budget.</p>
<p>Lawmakers are now in the final stages of wrapping work on an $8.59 billion general fund budget for fiscal 1998 beginning October 1.</p>
<p>Senators also advanced a plan to use $69 million of interest from the &quot;rainy day&quot; fund for road repairs during the current fiscal year.</p>
<p>((--David Bailey, Chicago Newsroom, 312-408-8647))</p>
